  "name": "Fengyang huagu (Anhui flower-drum song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song-and-drum performance of Fengyang in northern Anhui, carried for centuries by itinerant performers, often women, who sang while beating a small two-headed drum with a pair of thin sticks, partnered by a small-gong player; its best-known song, the 'Fengyang ge', laments the district's famine years. It is on the national intangible cultural heritage list (the acoustic_membrane_drum card stands in for the flower drum and the gong_tamtam card for the small gong).",
  "recipe": "classic modern fengyang huagu, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment. membrane drum pulse acoustic membrane drum, gong chau gong tamtam. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
